WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.450
- He does not look happy in these photos.

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:04.590
And I kind of do.

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:05.840
Well, I was really happy.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:08.912
Oh my God, I don't wanna cry.

00:00:08.912 --> 00:00:10.390
(participant laughs)

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.223
(mellow music)

00:00:11.223 --> 00:00:12.145
(notes whooshing)

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.370
(keyboard clacking)

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.010
- [Interviewer] Do you have any
texts from any of your exes?

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.000
- Yes, I do.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.080
- Yes, I do.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:19.913
- No, I don't.

00:00:19.913 --> 00:00:20.760
- All that's deleted.

00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:21.593
- I do.

00:00:21.593 --> 00:00:22.426
- Yes.

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:23.580
We were in an open relationship,

00:00:23.580 --> 00:00:24.810
which had been, you know,

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.090
fine for the almost year
that we were together.

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.470
You know, we were both very communicative,

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:29.670
very open and, you know,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:31.290
very accepting and willing to, you know,

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:32.730
discuss whatever was brought up.

00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:36.810
And, one evening he asked me that,

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:38.430
if he could see someone that, you know,

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.420
he had seen again.

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:40.475
He was like,

00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:41.760
"Hey, can I see so and so again,"

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:43.927
and it was the first
time where I was like,

00:00:43.927 --> 00:00:45.010
"No, sorry."

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:45.843
(participant laughs)

00:00:45.843 --> 00:00:46.920
We like, broke up.

00:00:46.920 --> 00:00:47.753
And I told him,

00:00:47.753 --> 00:00:48.586
I was like, "Cool.

00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:50.430
Just so you know, if you
start dating that person,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:51.300
I'm gonna kill you."

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.133
And he was like,

00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.370
"Oh, I'm not even thinking about that.

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.203
Like, what are you talking about?"

00:00:54.203 --> 00:00:55.036
You know, and I was just like,

00:00:55.036 --> 00:00:56.190
"Okay, whatever you say."

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.510
But I just, like,

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:59.910
let's make sure I'm establishing this now.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.830
And, then January came

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.610
and he basically told me that
he was seeing that person.

00:01:05.610 --> 00:01:10.173
And, I thought it would just
be best if we no longer spoke.

00:01:10.173 --> 00:01:11.006
(note whooshing)

00:01:11.006 --> 00:01:11.839
(keyboard clacking)

00:01:11.839 --> 00:01:13.080
"Hey, I'm not sure if you
check the Discord anymore,

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:14.940
but the last session for my campaign

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.890
is scheduled for the night of the 12th.

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:18.720
If you're free, we'd love to have you."

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:19.867
The second message was,

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:21.960
"Also if you haven't already heard,

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.950
that person and I have started
dating as of a few days ago.

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:26.310
I know you expressed

00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:28.290
that you would be unhappy
about that if it happened,

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.480
but I still wanted to be upfront about it.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:32.250
I hope you're feeling better from COVID

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.083
and I'm looking forward

00:01:33.083 --> 00:01:34.477
to potentially seeing you at D&amp;D."

00:01:34.477 --> 00:01:35.460
"That sounds nice

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.410
and I appreciate you
being straightforward,

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.906
but I can't lie, I am pretty upset.

00:01:39.906 --> 00:01:41.610
I think we shouldn't
talk for a little bit,

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:42.540
at least a month.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.940
I'm sorry, but I'm genuinely
at a loss for words.

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:46.590
I hope your grad school app went well.

00:01:46.590 --> 00:01:47.937
Have a great 2022."

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.090
Having someone who started as a friend,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.210
it sucks 'cause I'm like,

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.820
I'm not only losing a
partner, I'm losing a friend.

00:01:56.820 --> 00:01:58.743
It sucks to throw that away.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.970
- I caught my ex cheating on me.

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.310
And then when I confronted
him, he got violent.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:09.076
I realized I shouldn't be
in that situation anymore,

00:02:09.076 --> 00:02:10.980
so I just packed my bags and left

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:13.353
and I never looked back after that.

00:02:14.353 --> 00:02:16.200
And, for a couple weeks

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.480
he would just send me waves of texts.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.390
So it was first, "Hey, can we talk?"

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:23.340
And then the next day he says, "Please?"

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.540
At that point,

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.722
I didn't wanna talk to him

00:02:26.722 --> 00:02:28.740
because he cheated on me

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:30.540
and I just wanted to move on from there.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:31.380
I don't know how,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.780
I was single at this
point and I went on a date

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.730
and somehow he found out I went on a date.

00:02:35.730 --> 00:02:36.877
And so he texted me,

00:02:36.877 --> 00:02:38.970
"You went on a date with someone else?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.670
Already? Ivie, I loved you.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.870
I wanted to fix things

00:02:42.870 --> 00:02:45.701
and took time to gather
my thoughts and seek help.

00:02:45.701 --> 00:02:48.450
Everything we had, I (beep) up."

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.023
And then, in that same day,

00:02:50.023 --> 00:02:52.050
I felt something was off.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.637
And then I found his car
in front of my house.

00:02:54.637 --> 00:02:56.156
"I'm not here for your forgiveness.

00:02:56.156 --> 00:02:59.220
Just my stuff and to
talk it out and move on.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:00.053
That's it.

00:03:00.053 --> 00:03:02.640
I'm making a police report
tonight for stolen property.

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:03.780
I really don't want to,

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:05.490
but you're really forcing my hand here."

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:07.170
He said he's going to the police,

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:09.300
so I wouldn't be able to go to the police

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.890
to file a report for myself.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:12.630
I kind of felt lost at that point

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.980
and I didn't really know what to do.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:15.130
I just don't understand

00:03:17.657 --> 00:03:19.230
why someone's learning experience

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:23.490
has to come at the expense
of traumatizing others.

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.728
- As like, a younger gay kid,

00:03:25.728 --> 00:03:28.770
I'd always see TV shows of like,

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:30.852
this guy who got matched with like,

00:03:30.852 --> 00:03:33.840
this straight guy that they
didn't know they were gay

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:35.850
and it ended up like,

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.570
kindling into this fairytale
type of relationship.

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.790
I had ended up with a best friend

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.950
in high school my senior year.

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:46.140
It was a nice thing for
me having like, a friend.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:50.160
And I found myself getting
closer and closer to this guy.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.300
And I've never had like,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.270
a really close, best
friend that was a guy.

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:55.341
And I figured out why.

00:03:55.341 --> 00:03:56.174
(participant laughs)

00:03:56.174 --> 00:03:57.720
Because I'd end up
catching feelings for him.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:04:00.060
It was just really strange,

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:01.050
because he was a very like,

00:04:01.050 --> 00:04:03.360
Christian football player,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.880
go to church every Sunday.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.830
It was just very like,

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:08.850
difficult, I guess,

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:11.190
for him to process those emotions

00:04:11.190 --> 00:04:14.220
and overcoming of like, who you are.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.380
So, how we would hang out is

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:17.580
we wouldn't really like, text much.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.426
We would just text, oh,
do you want to hang out?

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:21.420
Yeah, sure.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.460
And then we'd like,
spend the day together.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:25.452
And then that's how we would
like, communicate a bunch.

00:04:25.452 --> 00:04:26.285
(keyboard clacking)

00:04:26.285 --> 00:04:29.640
"Hey, do you want to go
hang out and get some food?"

00:04:29.640 --> 00:04:30.473
No response.

00:04:30.473 --> 00:04:31.417
Like, a day passed.

00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:33.307
"Hey man, is everything all right?"

00:04:33.307 --> 00:04:34.200
"I don't know, man.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.007
I don't think we should
be doing this anymore."

00:04:36.007 --> 00:04:37.860
"Okay, that's fine.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:40.500
But, you're not gonna be pulling
this crap over text again.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:42.060
You're gonna tell me why to my face."

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.370
That kind of just led into the

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.607
in-person conversation
that we had the next day.

00:04:46.607 --> 00:04:49.110
'Cause I know he's still like,

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.100
figuring himself out.

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:53.130
He's still like, thinking
about his feelings for me.

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:54.420
And I just want to be like,

00:04:54.420 --> 00:04:56.610
you know, I love you.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:58.200
You had this and it was there,

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.820
but, I'm done with it.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.250
And I just kind of wanna
like, go on from that.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.080
I feel like I really just like,

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.900
gave up a part of my heart, I guess,

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:09.480
to someone that really
wasn't ready to receive it.

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.980
- We dated in high school

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:12.240
and then we had like,

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.460
a messy breakup when I
moved away for college.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.050
It was kind of something that I did.

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:18.600
I confronted his girl best friend

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.520
because I was uncomfortable
with their friendship.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.520
He would tell me like, oh,
you're just my girlfriend.

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.530
Like, you're not my best friend
'cause she's my best friend.

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.363
I didn't like that,

00:05:26.363 --> 00:05:29.790
so I traveled on the Greyhound to see him.

00:05:29.790 --> 00:05:32.943
And the second time that I came,

00:05:34.371 --> 00:05:35.204
he stood me up.

00:05:35.204 --> 00:05:37.020
Then unexpectedly, like two years later,

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.670
I get a text from a
random, unsaved number.

00:05:41.670 --> 00:05:43.119
And it was from him.

00:05:43.119 --> 00:05:43.952
(keyboard clacking)

00:05:43.952 --> 00:05:44.785
"I hope you're doing well.

00:05:44.785 --> 00:05:46.530
I don't wanna take too much of your time,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:47.700
but I need to let you know

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.880
that I'm in the process
of applying for a job

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.310
and they're doing a
background check on me.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.680
They requested your information
so I gave it to them

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.509
and they will probably call or email you.

00:05:57.509 --> 00:05:58.860
I know this is random,

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.237
but I still thought I should
let you know in advance."

00:06:01.237 --> 00:06:02.280
"Yeah, okay.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.740
Why would they ask for my info
in the first place, though?"

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.127
He responded with,

00:06:06.127 --> 00:06:07.650
"During my background interview,

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:09.690
they asked about my last relationships.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:11.430
And since you were my last serious one,

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.200
they wanted your info."

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.437
And then I responded with,

00:06:14.437 --> 00:06:16.500
"Oh, okay. LOL, yeah, no worries."

00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:18.000
And then right after that,

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:22.410
he sent me this
three-paragraph long message

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:24.870
about how he wanted to
get stuff off his chest

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.720
and basically kind of,
apologize for everything.

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:29.700
And honestly, I really
wanted that closure.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:30.750
That's why I like,

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:34.380
rode on the Greyhound
twice, 300 miles one way.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:35.213
I never got it,

00:06:35.213 --> 00:06:38.550
so it was the closure that
I needed two years ago,

00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:40.410
but I'm finally getting it.

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:42.120
- [Interviewer] Do you
have any photos or videos

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.710
of when you guys were together?

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.840
- Like, I'll have notifications
and it'll say like,

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:47.430
memories or highlights and it's like,

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.050
Disneyland 2018.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.250
- [Interviewer] What
goes through your head?

00:06:52.503 --> 00:06:53.880
- How blind I was,

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.910
'cause he does not look
happy in these photos.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.920
And I kind of do.

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:00.183
Well, I was really happy.

00:07:01.875 --> 00:07:04.557
As like, time went on,

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.333
his smile kind of faded.

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:09.372
Oh my God, I don't wanna cry.

00:07:09.372 --> 00:07:11.520
(participant laughs)

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:14.228
- She, actually, slid into my DMs.

00:07:14.228 --> 00:07:15.420
(Heischler laughs)

00:07:15.420 --> 00:07:18.420
She was a follower of me previously,

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:19.770
from my social media.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:23.820
And it was just a really toxic
relationship from the start.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:26.640
She became friends with
another one of my friends

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:30.570
and she added her on
her personal IG story.

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:35.250
And I guess she was out
one night and basically,

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:38.130
she was making out with a guy

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:41.220
and she posted it on her
close friend's story.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:43.080
And she posted it on her
close friend's story,

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.880
obviously, because I wasn't on there.

00:07:44.880 --> 00:07:48.690
But I guess she forgot
that she had my friend,

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:50.130
who I've known before her,

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:52.320
my friend screen-shotted
it and showed it to me

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.510
and was like, are you guys good?

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.280
I sent three question marks,

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:59.490
just 'cause I wanted to
see what she would say.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:02.130
And then she was like,
"Hi, babe. You okay?"

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.780
I could either play into this,

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:05.460
or I can just send you the screenshot

00:08:05.460 --> 00:08:06.570
and make you feel dumb.

00:08:06.570 --> 00:08:07.920
So that's exactly what I did.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:09.660
I just sent the screenshot.

00:08:09.660 --> 00:08:11.730
And I said, right after,

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:14.587
"So this is what you do on
your private stories, huh?"

00:08:14.587 --> 00:08:16.740
"I'm sorry, I was honestly so drunk,

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:20.190
I forgot to tell you that
I made out with a friend.

00:08:20.190 --> 00:08:22.290
This week has been so F'd up

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:24.867
and I needed to get out and have fun.

00:08:24.867 --> 00:08:26.970
I know I F'd up, I'm so sorry."

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:27.803
And so I said,

00:08:27.803 --> 00:08:29.754
"How do you forget to tell me

00:08:29.754 --> 00:08:31.980
but post it on your private story?

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:33.780
Did you forget that you had my friend

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:35.100
on your private story?"

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:35.933
Dot, dot, dot.

00:08:35.933 --> 00:08:38.430
And then, this is where
it gets interesting.

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.087
So she texted me,

00:08:40.087 --> 00:08:41.910
"Ima try to convince him."

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:43.080
And I was like,

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.430
that wasn't meant for me.

00:08:44.430 --> 00:08:45.263
And I said,

00:08:45.263 --> 00:08:47.250
"Oops, yeah, you're for the streets. Bye."

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:48.360
- [Interviewer] Do you hope to like,

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.240
have a new relationship
soon in the future?

00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:54.600
Or are you sort of waiting
and taking your time?

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.470
- I'm waiting.

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:57.924
Taking my time, focusing on me.

00:08:57.924 --> 00:08:59.580
You know? It's all about me.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.440
I'm in a relationship with myself.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.377
There we go.

00:09:02.377 --> 00:09:05.090
I'm in a relationship
with me, with Heischler.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:05.923
- Yeah.

00:09:05.923 --> 00:09:06.973
- [Interviewer] Nice.

